# EAS archives from the git root, so exclude everything that isn't the mobile
# app. The ml-research tree (ESC-50 dataset, spectrogram caches, trained models,
# denoised WAVs) is multiple GB and irrelevant to the Android build — including
# it made the upload tarball 654 MB and the upload kept dropping (ECONNRESET).

# --- Non-mobile parts of the repo (not needed to build the app) ---
ml-research/
services/
docs/
demo/

# --- Large/binary artifacts anywhere (the bundled *.tflite model is KEPT) ---
*.apk
*.aab
*.wav
*.m4a
*.keras
*.tflite.bak
*.ndjson
*.log

# The blanket *.wav above is aimed at the multi-GB ml-research corpus, but it
# also swallowed the one WAV the app bundles — SpectrogramTestScreen's
# "Play sample" button require()s it, so an EAS build without it fails to
# resolve the asset. Re-include just that file.
#
# Ordering matters: these are gitignore semantics, where the LAST matching
# pattern wins, so this negation must stay below `*.wav`. It works only because
# no parent directory of the file is itself excluded — gitignore cannot
# re-include a file underneath an excluded directory. Keep mobile/assets/ out
# of the exclusion list above or this silently stops working.
!mobile/assets/audio/snore-sample.wav

# --- Node / Expo ---
node_modules/
.expo/
.tunnels/

# --- Generated Android build artifacts (Windows abs paths break EAS's Linux
# workers; the worker regenerates them). ---
mobile/android/build/
mobile/android/.gradle/
mobile/android/.kotlin/
mobile/android/app/build/
mobile/android/app/.cxx/
